<title>UK: Licht details 96/97 world sugar output estimates.</title>
<headline>Licht details 96/97 world sugar output estimates.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a table of world sugar production for the 1996/97 crop year as forecast by German statistician F.O. Licht on Monday.</p>
<p>Figures are in thousands of tonnes, raw value.</p>
<p>     BEET SUGAR	  1996/97	    1995/96</p>
<p> France		    4,340		 4,601</p>
<p> Germany		   4,340		 4,155</p>
<p> Italy		     1,467		 1,621</p>
<p> Netherlands	     1,076		 1,074</p>
<p> Spain		     1,166		 1,196</p>
<p> United Kingdom	  1,413		 1,326</p>
<p> EU TOTAL		 16,858		17,005</p>
<p> Turkey		    2,011		 1,495</p>
<p> WEST EUROPE TOTAL    19,499		18,956</p>
<p> Poland		    2,170		 1,715</p>
<p> Russia		    1,820		 2,239</p>
<p> Ukraine		   3,150		 3,783</p>
<p> EAST EUROPE TOTAL     9,285		 9,707</p>
<p> US beet		   3,538		 3,583</p>
<p> China		     1,347		 1,403</p>
<p> Japan			 706		   707</p>
<p> WORLD BEET TOTAL     36,417		36,433</p>
<p>CANE SUGAR</p>
<p> Spain			   5		     5</p>
<p> Egypt		     1,097		 1,108</p>
<p> South Africa	    2,620		 1,791</p>
<p> AFRICA TOTAL	    8,398		 7,052</p>
<p> US mainland cane	2,448		 2,693</p>
<p> Cuba			4,800		 4,530</p>
<p> Guatemala		 1,460		 1,411</p>
<p> Mexico		    4,677		 4,758</p>
<p> N/C TOTAL		16,401		16,311</p>
<p> Argentina		 1,271		 1,620</p>
<p> Brazil		   15,022		13,636</p>
<p> Colombia		  2,111		 2,045</p>
<p> S/AMERICA TOTAL	20,806		19,522</p>
<p> China		     5,715		 5,367</p>
<p> India		    16,750		17,831</p>
<p> Indonesia		 2,478		 2,274</p>
<p> Pakistan		  3,150		 2,663</p>
<p> Philippines	     1,900		 1,775</p>
<p> Thailand		  6,750		 6,380</p>
<p> ASIA TOTAL	     38,478		38,088</p>
<p> Australia		 5,570		 5,133</p>
<p> OCEANIA total	   6,108		 5,652</p>
<p> WORLD CANE	     90,196		86,630</p>
<p> World TOTAL OUTPUT  126,613	     123,063</p>
